   "AnchorBarGrid"], Cell["Kinematics, References and On-Shell Conditions",
   "TechNoteTitle"], Cell["Keep external kinematics, channel residues and \
diagram numerator assumptions distinct.", "TechNoteText"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT", "ExampleSubsection"],
     Cell["Evaluate this setup once before the examples. The paths refer to \
the local HEPCAT checkout; no model parameters are assigned global numerical \
values.", "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"If", "[", "!", "StringQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", " ", "||", " ", "!", "DirectoryQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", ",", "\n", " ", " ",
         "Global`$HEPCATpath", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{",
         "First", "[", "PacletFind", "[", "\"HEPCAT\"", "]", "]", "[",
         "\"Location\"", "]", ",", " ", "\"source\"", "}", "]", "]", ";",
         "\n", "If", "[", "!", "MemberQ", "[", "$Packages", ",", " ",
         "\"ConstructiveDiagrams`\"", "]", ",", "\n", " ", " ", "Get", "[",
         "FileNameJoin", "[", "{", "Global`$HEPCATpath", ",", " ",
         "\"HEPCAT.wl\"", "}", "]", "]", "]", ";", "\n", "hepcatDirectory",
         " ", "=", " ", "ParentDirectory", "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]",
         ";", "\n", "modelDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[",
         "{", "hepcatDirectory", ",", " ", "\"models\"", "}", "]", ";", "\n",
         "feynmanModelDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{",
         "hepcatDirectory", ",", " ", "\"model_feynman\"", "}", "]", ";"}]],
      "Input", InitializationCell -> True]}, Open]],
  Cell["All External Momenta Are Incoming", "TechNoteSection"],
  Cell["HEPCAT analytic formulas obey p1 + p2 + ... = 0 with every external \
momentum incoming. Reordering particles changes labels; crossing reverses a \
momentum and its spinor conventions. Use ReverseMomentum for symbolic \
crossing and give WriteSPINASProcess the physical incoming-to-outgoing \
process.", "TechNoteText"], Cell["For the angle/square convention used here, \
a crossed massless momentum reverses the angle spinor sign while the square \
spinor is unchanged. Do not reverse only Mom insertions and leave its spinors \
unchanged.", "TechNoteText"], Cell["External and Internal Conditions",
   "TechNoteSection"], Cell["ReduceSpinorProducts uses ordinary spinor \
identities and external mass algebra. Process-wide momentum conservation is \
handled in PrepareAmplitudes, where the process labels are available.",
   "TechNoteText"], Cell["A diagram pair carries a mass replacement list. An \
internal entry records a numerator condition for that diagram. \
PrepareAmplitudes can use it aggressively while preserving discarded \
remainders in the detailed report. PropDen objects keep the actual \
propagators off shell.", "TechNoteText"], Cell["A factorization channel puts \
its cut momentum on shell when its residue is compared with a product of \
lower-point amplitudes. It does not put every internal line of the \
lower-point amplitudes on shell.", "TechNoteText"],
  Cell["A final amplitude with an external mass list can be prepared again. \
Without internal entries, preparation must not invent diagram-specific \
internal conditions. Feynman diagram internals remain off shell throughout.",
   "TechNoteText"], Cell["Reference Choices", "TechNoteSection"],
  Cell["PolePreference controls reference choices and biases later \
representation searches. AllSpurious uses suitable massless references when \
available; AllPhysical uses spinor-momentum references that create admissible \
physical denominators; Mixed searches both kinds. Automatic chooses from the \
supported choices.", "TechNoteText"], Cell["Constructive diagram \
representatives may use different reference choices while completion restores \
the required full-channel constraints. Feynman diagrams are not separately \
gauge invariant, so their full sum must use a consistent external reference \
assignment.", "TechNoteText"], Cell["Reference independence of the final \
result is a real test. Leaving an unresolved xi in an expression is not \
automatically a failure, but the checker must vary admissible reference \
spinors and compare the complete amplitude.", "TechNoteText"],
  Cell["Related Functions", "SeeAlsoSection"],
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["ReverseMomentum", BaseStyle -> "Link",
      ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/ref/ReverseMomentum"], "  \[Bullet]  ",
     ButtonBox["PermuteParticles", BaseStyle -> "Link",
      ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/ref/PermuteParticles"], "  \[Bullet]  ",
